Credits
-------

Amiga port, GUI front-ends, skin engine, decoder integration, internet
radio, artwork and m68k/68060 optimisation by Darren Banfi (boingball).

Audio decoder components:

  - MP3: Helix fixed-point decoder from RealNetworks
  - AAC: Helix AAC through ESP8266Audio by Earle F. Philhower III
  - FLAC: libfoxenflac by Alexander Stoeckel
  - Ogg Vorbis: Xiph.Org Tremor via Phil Schatzmann's Arduino port,
    together with Xiph.Org libogg
  - WMA: Rockbox fixed-point libwma, derived from FFmpeg's WMA decoder

Artwork decoder components:

  - JPEG: picojpeg-compatible decoder; picojpeg was created by Rich Geldreich
  - PNG: LodePNG by Lode Vandevenne
  - WebP: compact implementation using parts of Google's libwebp reference
    decoder under its BSD licence

Winamp is a trademark of its respective owner. MintAMP reads the classic
.wsz skin format; it contains no Winamp code. The bundled mint-leaf skin
was made for MintAMP.

The MintAMP-specific skin engine, ASF/WMA integration, WAV/PCM and IFF-8SVX
decoders, and ICO, SVG and compact WebP artwork handlers were developed with
assistance from Anthropic Claude and OpenAI Codex.

These components remain under their respective licences, including the Helix
RPSL, LGPL, BSD-style and LodePNG terms. See the licence files and source
repository for the complete terms and source code.

Support: https://buymeacoffee.com/boingball

History
-------

2.0    Classic Winamp 2.x skin support. MintAMP-SR (ReAction) and
       MintAMP-SGT (GadTools) open with the bundled mint-leaf skin and
       load any classic .wsz skin, at normal or double size, with skinned
       playlist, equaliser, artwork and settings windows, windowshade
       mode and Winamp-style keys.
       A Classic interface menu tick switches the running player between
       the skin and the classic MintAMP window without stopping playback,
       and is remembered for the next launch.
       New MintAMP-Launch starts the chosen edition and appearance, set
       by Interface preferences, ToolTypes or the command line.
       Spectrum analyser and oscilloscope, timed to the audio you hear.
       MP3 equaliser, balance, shuffle and repeat. Play, Eject and the
       playlist work as in Winamp.
       Internet radio: you can now search, browse favourites and change
       station while a stream is playing, and the radio window's status
       line shows Buffering, Streaming, Stopped or the reason a stream
       failed, instead of staying on Buffering.
       A file that cannot be played now says why ("Can't play: ...") in
       the status line and skin title: video-only files, WMA Pro,
       Lossless and Voice, MP4/M4A AAC, a missing decoder or a missing
       file.
       Faster 68060 MP3 (hardware multiplies in IMDCT, anti-alias,
       stereo and dequantisation; DCT and low-band paths) and AAC
       transforms, making 14700 Hz output affordable on a 68060.
       Playback timing and statistics use integer maths throughout.
       Fixed: FLAC, Ogg, WMA, WAV and AAC files lost their last 8-10
       seconds; WMA decoded only part of each packet, and WMA files
       with video failed at the end of the audio; about 36 KB of memory
       was lost every time a GUI edition was started.

1.4.0  Lossless FLAC internet radio, including FLAC inside Ogg. Station
       links that point at a .pls or .m3u playlist now play, with
       fallback to the next server. Playlists can hold radio stations as
       well as files and load and save .pls as well as .m3u. Radio
       favourites can be bookmarked from the playing stream, renamed,
       removed, reordered, exported and imported; up to 50 are kept.
       Station names and titles are converted for Latin-1 fonts.
       Numerous radio, FLAC and AAC fixes.

1.3.2  Builds again with the GCC 13 Amiga toolchain as well as GCC 16.

1.3.1  MPEG-2.5 MP3 files (8, 11.025 and 12 kHz) now play. Faster 68060
       AAC noise substitution and TNS. RadioInfo XML song titles.
       Double-click a station in the radio browser to play it.

1.3.0  CPU-specific AAC, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis and WMA math helpers, with
       hardware-only multiplies in the 68060 edition.

1.2.0  Workbench AppIcon iconification. Expanded GadTools radio browser.
       Refined GadTools layouts. Fast RAM preload for all local formats.

1.1.0  Dedicated 68060 drawer. Improved HTTP/HTTPS radio throughput and
       buffering. Station artwork improvements.

1.0.0  Initial Aminet release.
